language and backend. Preserve its definition, ordered ABI, numerical requirements,
execution target and every workload.

Read the action layout when needed: `from klineage.prompts import action_spec`;
inspect `action_spec("generation")` with `klineage.serialization.raw_text`.

{% set generation = true %}
{% set target_language = problem.language %}
{% include "backend.j4" %}

Read workspace/.agents/skills/bench/SKILL.md for correctness and timing.

# Procedure

1. Inspect the Problem's definition, reference implementation and all workloads.
   Derive the ordered inputs, outputs, shapes and data types. Query the backend's
   kernel layout and read relevant examples when needed.

2. Write current_kernel/metadata.json and current_kernel/submission/ with a simple
   implementation. Its entry function owns launch parameters. Submit it
   with klineage.evaluate(Path("current_kernel")). Obtain an accepted
   result across every workload before optional performance experiments.

3. Improve the implementation within the remaining time. Evaluate each edited
   candidate against the problem oracle with reference=None. Read each workload's
   correctness, latency and diagnostics; keep the replies for accepted candidates.

4. Finish with the best accepted candidate as the last numbered versions/<N>/.
   Select an earlier accepted job with klineage.result(best_reply)
   when needed; it appends that measured Kernel as the latest version. Leave
   saved versions unchanged and explain the implementation and measurements
   in the final response. Produce a Kernel only.
